==English==

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|back|light}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbæk.laɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-backlight.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[light|Light]] shining from a source behind the object of interest or attention.
#: {{ux|en|The '''backlight''' from the sunset cast the pier and the crowd in silhouette.}}
#: {{ux|en|Egg candling uses '''backlight''' to look for chick embryos.}}
## {{lb|en|countable}} A [[spotlight]] that [[illuminate]]s a [[photographic]] [[subject]] from [[behind]].
## {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[light|Light]] that is behind a photographic subject.
##* {{quote-book|en|title=Lighting and the Dramatic Portrait|publisher=Amphoto Books|author=w:Michael Grecco|year=2006|ISBN=9780817442279|page=73
|passage=If I do use '''backlight''', it's not to separate the subject from the background; I use it to set a psychological mood, or to create a look.}}
## {{lb|en|countable}} A [[light]] attached to an [[LCD]] [[display]].
# {{lb|en|countable}} The [[rear]] [[window]] of a [[motor car]].

